For a better insight into the mechanism of PMS activation over $\mathbf{Fe_{x}M n_{6-x}C o_{4}-N_{(o)}C}$ nano-dices, a number of characterizations on the used catalyst were carried out to clarify the structural changes and the redox cycling of the Fe, Co and Mn species during the reaction process. The XRD patterns of $\mathbf{Fe}_{1}\mathbf{Mn}_{5}\mathbf{Co}_{4}–\mathbf{N}_{}@\mathbf{C}$ before and after reaction are shown in Figure S14, while negligible changes could be found on the diffraction peaks of FeCo and $\bf{M n}_{4}\bf{N}$ . More importantly, the morphology of $\mathbf{Fe}_{1}\mathbf{Mn}_{5}\mathbf{Co}_{4}–\mathbf{N}_{}@\mathbf{C}$ was remained well (Figure S15). All these results suggest the good stability of the $\mathbf{Fe_{x}M n}_{6}$ - $\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathbf{x}}\mathbf{C}\mathbf{o}_{4}{-}\mathbf{N}(\widehat{\varrho}\mathbf{C}$ nano-dices.
High resolution XPS spectra of the used catalyst were applied to further explore the PMS activation mechanism. Figure 5A shows the high resolution XPS spectra of Co $2p_{3/2}$ of $\mathbf{Fe}_{1}\mathbf{Mn}_{5}\mathbf{Co}_{4}–\mathbf{N}_{}@\mathbf{C}$ before and after the reaction. Three peaks with binding energy located at 778.5, 780.5 and 782.1 eV could be assigned to the alloyed cobalt $({\bf C o}^{0}),{\bf C o}^{2+},$ , and ${\bf C o}^{3+}$ , respectively.56, 57 After the reaction, the peak of ${\bf C o}^{0}$ disappeared and the relative contents of ${\bf C o}^{2+}$ and ${\bf C o}^{3+}$ increased. Similar phenomenon was found on the high resolution XPS spectra of Fe $2p_{3/2}$ of $\mathbf{Fe}_{1}\mathbf{Mn}_{5}\mathbf{Co}_{4}–\mathbf{N}_{\widehat{(a)}}\mathbf{C}$ (Figure S16). All these results suggest that the ${\bf C o}^{0}$ and $\boldsymbol{\mathrm{Fe}^{0}}$ on $\mathbf{Fe}_{1}\mathbf{Mn}_{5}\mathbf{Co}_{4}–\mathbf{N}_{}@\mathbf{C}$ surface were oxidized during the activation of PMS. The high resolution XPS spectra of N 1s of the catalyst before and after the reaction are shown in Figure 5B. Negligible changes could be found on the nitrogen bound to the metal ( $\mathbf{Mn-N}$ and Fe-N), as well as the pyridinic $\mathbf{N}$ and graphitic N, indicating the better stability of $\mathbf{Mn}_{4}\mathbf{N}$ for the activation of PMS. The XPS spectra of Mn $2p_{3/2}$ (Figure 5C) could be deconvoluted into three contribu
