tions with binding energy located at 639.5, 641.3, and $643.1\ \mathrm{eV};$ , attributed to the metallic manganese $(\mathbf{M}\mathbf{n}^{0})$ , $\mathbf{M}\mathbf{n}^{2+}$ , and $\mathbf{M}\mathbf{n}^{3+}$ , respectively.8, 58 The relative proportion of $\mathbf{M}\mathbf{n}^{0}$ was decreased after reaction, suggesting the partial oxidation of $\mathbf{M}\mathbf{n}^{0}$ to $\mathbf{M}\mathbf{n}^{2+}$ , and $\mathbf{M}\mathbf{n}^{3+}$ on $\mathbf{Fe}_{1}\mathbf{Mn}_{5}\mathbf{Co}_{4}.$ - $\mathbf{N}@\mathbf{C}$ surface. In addition, the increase of the relative proportion of lattice $^{\circ}$ after reaction (Figure 5d) could further confirmed the oxidation of $\mathbf{Co^{0}},\mathbf{Fe^{0}}.$ , and $\mathbf{M}\mathbf{n}^{0}$ during the activation of PMS. However, still $12\%$ of the relative contributions of $\mathbf{M}\mathbf{n}^{0}$ to the overall Mn intensity after reaction further suggest the better stability of $\bf{M n}_{4}\bf{N}$ for the activation of PMS.
Therefore, the overall mechanism of PMS activation over $\mathbf{Fe_{x}M n_{6-x}C o_{4}-N}\boldsymbol{\mathcal{O}}\mathbf{C}$ nano-dices could be proposed as following (Figure 6). Firstly, $\equiv{\bf C o}^{0}/{\bf F e}^{0}/{\bf M}{\bf n}^{0}$ in $\mathbf{Fe_{x}M n_{6-x}C o_{4}-N}\boldsymbol{\ @}\mathbf{C}$ could activate PMS to produce $s\mathrm{O}_{4}$ •- and •OH radicals through Eqs. 1,2 with itself oxidized to $\equiv{\bf C o}^{2+}/{\bf F e}^{2+}/{\bf M}{\bf n}^{2+}$ and $\equiv{\bf C o}^{3+}/{\bf F e}^{3+}/{\bf M}{\bf n}^{3+}$ , respectively.17, 44 Secondly, the generated $\equiv\mathrm{Co}^{2+}/\mathrm{Fe}^{2+}/\mathrm{Mn}^{2+}$ could be quickly oxidized by PMS and produced $s\mathrm{O}_{4}..\mathrm{\Delta}$ radicals (Eq. 3). Both PMS and $\equiv{\bf C o}^{0}/{\bf F e}^{0}/{\bf M}{\bf n}^{0}$ could further reduce $\equiv{\bf C o}^{3+}/{\bf F e}^{3+}/{\bf M}{\bf n}^{3+}$ to $\equiv\mathrm{Co}^{2+}/\mathrm{Fe}^{2+}/\mathrm{Mn}^{2+}$ and thus makes the reaction proceed cyclically until PMS was completely consumed.59-61 In addition, the stronger $E_{\mathrm{ads}},$ longer $l_{0-0},$ and more electrons received on PMS catalyzed by $\mathbf{Mn}_{4}\mathbf{N}$ , largely enhanced the catalytic activity of $\mathbf{Fe_{x}M n_{6-x}C o_{4}-N_{(o)}C}$ .
