## CONCLUSIONS
In summary, topotactic transformation was developed as a facile strategy for shape-controlled synthesis of graphene encapsulated TMNs $\mathbf{\tilde{\Gamma}}(\mathbf{Fe_{x}M n_{6-x}C o_{4}}\mathbf{-N}(\mathbf{\overline{{{\alpha}}}})\mathbf{C})$ via a one-step thermal decomposition of MOFs in ${\bf N}_{2}$ atmosphere. The catalytic oxidation performance of the assynthesized $\mathbf{Fe_{x}M n_{6-x}C o_{4}-N}\boldsymbol{\mathcal{Q}}\mathbf{C}$ nano-dices in BPA degradation by PMS activation was found largely enhanced with the increasing of the content of $\bf{M n}_{4}\bf{N}$ . The optimal activity of $\mathbf{Fe}_{1}\mathbf{Mn}_{5}\mathbf{Co}_{4}–\mathbf{N}_{\widehat{(a)}}\mathbf{C}$ was much higher than that of $\mathbf{Fe}_{1}\mathbf{Mn}_{5}\mathbf{Co}_{4}–\mathbf{H}\textcircled{\alpha}\mathbf{C}$ which contains MnO and FeCo alloy as the main phase. DFT calculations illustrated that $\bf{M n}_{4}\bf{N}$ is able to dramatically reduce the adsorption energy and facilitate electron transfer for PMS activation.
Through radical scavenger and EPR/DMPO experiments, both •OH and $\mathrm{{}}S O_{4}\bullet^{\cdot}$ were confirmed as the main reactive radicals involved during the PMS activation. Moreover, the overall PMS activation mechanism over $\mathbf{Fe_{x}M n_{6-x}C o_{4}{-N}}\mathbf{\widehat{\Gamma}}_{0}\mathbf{c}$ was proposed based on the systematic characterization of the catalyst before and after the reaction. This study details the insights into versatile TMNs for sustainable remediation by activation of PMS and may shed some light for the development of highperformance catalyst for PMS activation.
## EXPERIMENTAL METHODS
Chemicals. Potassium hexacyanocobaltate(III) $(98\%)$ was purchased from Beijing J&K Co., Ltd, China. PMS $\big(\mathrm{KHSO}_{5}{\bullet}0.5\mathrm{KHSO}_{4}{\bullet}0.5\mathrm{K}_{2}\mathrm{SO}_{4}\big)$ was purchased from Alfa Aesar. BPA, $p$ -hydroxybenzoic acid (HBA), benzoquinone (BQ) and 5,5-dimethyl-1-pyrroline-N-oxide (DMPO) were purchased from Aladdin Co., China. Ferrous chloride, manganous nitrate, tbutanol (TBA), methyl alcohol and poly(vinylpyrrolidone) (PVP) were purchased from Tianjin Kermel Chemical Reagent Co., Ltd, China.
Sample preparation. $\mathrm{Mn}_{\mathrm{y}}\mathrm{Fe}_{1-\mathrm{y}}\mathrm{\left[Co\left(CN\right)_{6}\right]}_{0.67\bullet\mathrm{nH}_{2}\mathrm{O}}$ $\mathbf{\dot{M}n_{y}F e_{1\cdot y^{-}}}$ Co PBAs; $0<\mathbf{y}<1\dot{}$ ) were synthesized similarly to our previous report.8 Typically, desired amounts of $\mathrm{FeCl_{2}}{\bullet}4\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}$ and $\displaystyle\mathbf{M}\mathbf{n}(\mathbf{N}\mathbf{O}_{3})_{2}$ $\mathbf{\omega}(9\mathbf{\mM})$ were first dissolved in $40~\mathrm{mL}$ PVP $(1.2~\mathrm{g})$ solution under vigorous stirring. $40~\mathrm{mL}$ $\mathrm{K}_{3}[\mathrm{Co}(\mathrm{CN})_{6}]$ aqueous solution $({\boldsymbol{\mathsf{S}}}{\mathrm{~mM}})$ was then added into the above-mentioned solution slowly. The colloid solution was stirred for $30~\mathrm{min}$ and then aged for $20\mathrm{~h~}$ . The precipitates final obtained were centrifuged and washed for at least three times using the mixture of deionized water and ethanol, followed by drying at $333\mathrm{K}$ in an oven for $20\mathrm{h}$ $\mathbf{Fe_{x}M n_{6-x}C o_{4}-N_{(\mathcal{O})}C}$ $\begin{array}{r}{\mathbf{\tilde{\rho}}0<\mathbf{x}<6\mathbf{\dot{\rho}},}\end{array}$ ) and $\mathbf{Fe1Mn_{5}C o_{4}}–\mathbf{H}@\mathbf{C}$ nano-dices were obtained by heating $\mathbf{Mn}_{\mathrm{y}}\mathbf{Fe}_{\mathrm{1-y}}$ -Co PBAs at $650~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ and kept for $^{\textrm{1h}}$ under ${\bf N}_{2}$ and $\mathbf{H}_{2}$ atmosphere, respectively.
Catalytic activity measurements. The performance of the catalysts were tested in a $200~\mathrm{mL}$ reactor containing $20{\mathrm{~mg~L^{-1}}}$ BPA with a initial solution $\mathtt{p H}$ of 6.0. The reaction temperature was maintained at $25~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ using a water bath. In a typical test, $50~\mathrm{mL}$ BPA solution containing $\textrm{\textbf{5}m g}$ catalyst was first stirred for $10~\mathrm{{min}}$ to establish the adsorption-desorption equilibrium. A certain amount of PMS aqueous solution was then added into the abovementioned solution to initiate the reaction. $1{\mathrm{~mL}}$ solution was immediately withdrawn and quenched with $0.5{\mathrm{~mL}}$ methanol at
## ACS Nano
predetermined time intervals. The BPA and BQ concentration was analyzed using a high performance liquid chromatography (HPLC, Agilent, 1260-Infinity) at a detection wavelength of 230 and $244~\mathrm{nm}$ , respectively. Methanol/water mixture $\left(70{:}30,\ \nu/\nu\right)$ was used as the mobile phase. The BPA degradation intermediates were detected using LC-MS with an Agilent 1290 Infinity ultrahigh-performance liquid chromatography system equiped with an Agilent C18 column in combination with an Agilent 6540 quadrupole time-of-flight mass spectrometer. The total organic carbon (TOC) were detected by a total organic carbon analyzer (TOCVCPH/CPN, Shimadzu, Japan).
Computational models and methodology. The DFT calculations are carried out using CASTEP module.33 Exchangecorrelation functions are used as local density approximation (LDA) with CA$\mathrm{PZ}.^{34,35}$ The convergence tolerance of energy is $2.0\mathrm{e}^{-5}~\mathrm{eV/Atom}_{\cdot}$ , and the maximum allowed displacement and force are $0.002\mathring{\mathbf{A}}$ and $0.05\mathrm{eV}/{\mathring{\mathrm{A}}},$ , respectively. Considering the van der Waals forces, the DFT-D method is used for all calculations.36 To avoid the interaction of surfaces in different supercells along C direction, a 20 Å vacuum above the surface is taken. All atoms are allowed to relax expected the bottom one layer atoms to represent the bulk material surface.
